   "title": "IDEA-001 · Follow one box from Shenzhen to a customer",
   "original_idea": "[IDEA-001] Follow one box from Shenzhen to a customer\nCarousel · Visibility · 2026-11-11\n\nObjective:\nLife of a Box · answers How · Dark theme · Instagram + LinkedIn\n\nHook (EN):\nFollow one box.\n\nHook (AR):\nتابع كرتونة وحدة.\n\nScene plan:\nSupport line (EN):\nFrom a factory in Shenzhen to your customer's hands.\n\nOn-image elements (HTML layer):\nOne story across 7 slides; a small \"Day X\" kicker on every slide; the same box highlighted with a teal outline in each scene.\n\nSlides (carousels):\n1. Follow one box. — From a factory in Shenzhen to your customer's hands. [SC-08]\n2. Day 0 · Shenzhen — The supplier's invoice arrives. Stacko reads it and creates the items. [BG-58 + invoice card]\n3. Day 30 · Port of Beirut — The doors open. The box is already in the system. [SC-08]\n4. Day 32 · On the road — A transfer to Zahle. Everyone sees the ETA. [SC-01 + ETA tag]\n5. Day 32 · On the shelf — Stock lands on arrival. Nobody types it twice. [SC-05 + \"Restocked ✓\" chip on the gap]\n6. Day 33 · Sold — The right item, in the right branch, at the right time. [LCH-09]\n7. Every box has a story. — Stacko writes it down. [BG-56 + full footer]\n\nImages:\nSC-08 · BG-58 · SC-01 · SC-05 · LCH-09 · BG-56\n\nNotes:\nFlagship carousel: pin it to the profile.\n\nCaption:\nEvery box in your warehouse made a long journey to get there. Most systems only notice it at the very end.\nSwipe to follow one box from Shenzhen to a customer in Zahle, and see where Stacko steps in.\nWhich step loses the most time in your business?",
