   "original_idea": "[IDEA-013] Why we put stock on a map\nCarousel · Visibility · 2027-02-10\n\nObjective:\nFounder POV · answers Why · Dark theme · LinkedIn\n\nHook (EN):\nWhy we put stock on a map, not a table.\n\nHook (AR):\nليش حطّينا المخزون على خريطة؟\n\nScene plan:\nSupport line (EN):\nA note from the team behind Stacko.\n\nOn-image elements (HTML layer):\nText-led slides; slide 1 on BG-58, the rest on BG-60; small \"From the founder\" kicker.\n\nSlides (carousels):\n1. Why we put stock on a map, not a table.\n2. Tables don't show movement. Stock moves every day.\n3. Teams skip logging when nothing visible happens.\n4. On a map, every log moves a truck. That's the payoff.\n5. Logging becomes the reward, not the chore.\n\nImages:\nBG-58 · BG-60\n\nNotes:\nFounder voice: confirm wording with Nabih.\n\nCaption:\nWhen we started Stacko, the first client had three warehouses and one problem: nobody logged anything.\nThe fix wasn't a better table. It was making every log visible.\nWhat would make your team log?",
