   "title": "IDEA-033 · How does the truck know where it is?",
   "original_idea": "[IDEA-033] How does the truck know where it is?\nCarousel · Visibility · 2027-02-27\n\nObjective:\nTransparency · answers How · Dark theme · LinkedIn\n\nHook (EN):\nHow does the truck on the map know where it is?\n\nHook (AR):\nكيف الشاحنة عالخريطة بتعرف وين صارت؟\n\nScene plan:\nSupport line (EN):\nAn honest look under the hood.\n\nOn-image elements (HTML layer):\nSlide 1 on SC-01, rest on BG-58 with a simple progress-bar diagram.\n\nSlides (carousels):\n1. How does the truck on the map know where it is?\n2. It doesn't need GPS.\n3. It knows when the transfer left and when it should arrive.\n4. So it moves along the route as time passes, with a live countdown.\n5. GPS tracking comes later. The logging habit starts now.\n\nImages:\nSC-01 · BG-58\n\nNotes:\nFactual per the Product Bible (GPS is phase 2).\n\nCaption:\nPeople ask us if Stacko tracks trucks by GPS. Not yet, and it doesn't need to.\nDeparture time + ETA = a truck that moves on the map and a countdown everyone trusts.",
   "input_source": "csv",
   "source_reference": "Stacko_Content_Bank_New_Images.xlsx › Content › IDEA-033",
